From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MIRAGE <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:49:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] MIRAGE: one login is one host

Every channel of a connection (each exec request, the shell, SFTP) asked
the connection's server for a file system and was given a new one. A
directory made by one command was gone for the next command of the same
login, and a file put by SFTP was never there for the shell, though the
server object's own comment says that is what it is for. Found by the
suite's consistency group.

The file system is now made once for a connection, and the change
journal belongs to it: a later channel carries on with the journal, with
how far the responder has been sent it, and with the count of tokens the
login's answers have used.
